meta {
  name: 04 - OrderBy Direction Probe
  type: graphql
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}
  body: graphql
  auth: inherit
}

body:graphql {
  query OrderByDirectionProbe {
    byUpdated: users(first: 10, orderBy: updatedAt) { nodes { name updatedAt } }
    byCreated: users(first: 10, orderBy: createdAt) { nodes { name createdAt } }
    noOrderBy: users(first: 10) { nodes { name createdAt } }
  }
}

docs {
  Reference: https://linear.app/developers/pagination

  THE decisive probe for this cluster. `PaginationOrderBy` carries no direction modifier,
  and request `02 - Introspect Pagination Args` showed both enum members have a NULL
  description — so sort direction is undocumented in the prose docs AND absent from the
  schema. Direction dictates the entire cursor design:

  - ASCENDING would let a `filter.updatedAt.gt` sweep checkpoint after EVERY page, since
    everything before the last-seen `updatedAt` is known-read.
  - DESCENDING means the newest change arrives on page 1 and the oldest on the last page.
    Per-page checkpointing would then advance the cursor PAST records not yet read, and a
    crash mid-sweep would permanently skip everything between the old cursor and the
    last-emitted page.

  **Why `users` and not one of the four cluster streams:** this workspace was bulk-seeded,
  so all 4 issues and all 3 labels share the byte-identical `updatedAt`
  `2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z`. With every sort key tied, ascending and descending responses
  are indistinguishable — verified: `issues(sort: [{updatedAt: {order: Ascending}}])` and
  its `Descending` twin returned the exact same node order. `users` is the only collection
  in this workspace with DISTINCT timestamps (two members, seeded ~3s apart), which makes
  it the only available oracle. Direction is a property of the shared `PaginationOrderBy`
  enum, not of any one root field, so the result generalizes to all four cluster streams.

  **Limitation / observed finding:** `orderBy` sorts **DESCENDING** (newest first), for
  both enum members. Confirmed 2026-07-30 — see the saved example: `byUpdated` returns
  Jonathan Wihl (`...07.083Z`) before Linear (`...04.497Z`), and `byCreated` returns Linear
  (`...04.399Z`) before Jonathan (`...03.808Z`). `noOrderBy` is byte-identical to
  `byCreated`, confirming the documented default of `createdAt` — also descending.

  Consequence for the connector: any stream that can only use `orderBy` (i.e. `issueLabels`,
  which rejects the `sort` argument — see `42 - Labels Sort Rejected`) is restricted to
  END-OF-SWEEP checkpointing. Streams that accept `sort` should use
  `sort: [{updatedAt: {order: Ascending}}]` instead and may checkpoint per page.
}

example {
  name: 200 — DESCENDING confirmed (newest first)

  request: {
    url: https://api.linear.app/graphql
    method: POST
    mode: graphql

    body:graphql: {
      query OrderByDirectionProbe {
        byUpdated: users(first: 10, orderBy: updatedAt) { nodes { name updatedAt } }
        byCreated: users(first: 10, orderBy: createdAt) { nodes { name createdAt } }
        noOrderBy: users(first: 10) { nodes { name createdAt } }
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    headers: {
      x-complexity: 36
      x-ratelimit-requests-limit: 2500
      x-ratelimit-requests-remaining: 2496
      x-ratelimit-complexity-limit: 3000000
      x-ratelimit-complexity-remaining: 2999930
    }

    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }

    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "byUpdated": {
              "nodes": [
                {
                  "name": "Jonathan Wihl",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T21:35:07.083Z"
                },
                {
                  "name": "Linear",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T21:35:04.497Z"
                }
              ]
            },
            "byCreated": {
              "nodes": [
                {
                  "name": "Linear",
                  "createdAt": "2026-07-30T21:35:04.399Z"
                },
                {
                  "name": "Jonathan Wihl",
                  "createdAt": "2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z"
                }
              ]
            },
            "noOrderBy": {
              "nodes": [
                {
                  "name": "Linear",
                  "createdAt": "2026-07-30T21:35:04.399Z"
                },
                {
                  "name": "Jonathan Wihl",
                  "createdAt": "2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
